fullscreen vim scrollback mode, where mid-turn `Esc` is a no-op; minimal mode cancels even with vim on); `Ctrl+C` cancels once the composer is empty — with a draft, the first press only clears it. Idle, press `Esc` twice within 800ms to clear a non-empty prompt, or (with an empty prompt and conversation messages) to open rewind — see [Keyboard Shortcuts](03-keyboard-shortcuts.md#escape). With the scrollback focused, use the arrow keys to select entries and to collapse or expand them. To navigate with `j`/`k` and fold with `h`/`l` instead, enable Vim mode."},{"line_number":130,"content":"Collapse or expand the selected entry with the `Left`/`Right` arrow keys (or `h`/`l` and `e` in Vim mode). In Vim mode, press `y` to copy its content and `Y` to copy its metadata (for example, the command that ran). Press `Enter` to open it in the fullscreen viewer (in any mode)."}]},{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.grok\\docs\\user-guide\\03-keyboard-shortcuts.md","matches":[{"line_number":12,"content":"- **Vim mode** (opt-in): `j`/`k` for navigation, `H`/`L` for turn navigation, `J`/`K` for response navigation, `h`/`l` for fold, `e`/`E` for expand/collapse, and `i`/`Tab`/`Space` to focus the prompt."},{"line_number":61,"content":"| `h` | `Left` | Collapse selected entry |"},{"line_number":63,"content":"| `e` | | Toggle fold on selected entry |"},{"line_number":64,"content":"| `⇧E` | | Expand all / collapse all entries |"},{"line_number":65,"content":"| `Ctrl+E` | | Expand/collapse all thinking blocks |"},{"line_number":68,"content":"Setting `respect_manual_folds = true` under `[scrollback.scroll]` in"},{"line_number":70,"content":"[Configuration](05-configuration.md)) makes a hand-folded block pinned:"},{"line_number":202,"content":"> **Windows (non–VS Code family)**: Some consoles drop the `Ctrl` modifier on `Ctrl+Enter` (it can collapse to bare `Enter` or `Ctrl+J`). Use `Ctrl+I` as the alt — letter-key Ctrl chords are stable everywhere. On VS Code family, use **`Ctrl+L`**."},{"line_number":316,"content":"Folding:          h/l (collapse/expand)  e (toggle)  E (all)"}]},{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.grok\\docs\\user-guide\\04-slash-commands.md","matches":[{"line_number":211,"content":"The shell also advertises individual `/hooks-list`, `/hooks-trust`, `/hooks-add`, `/hooks-remove`, and `/hooks-untrust` commands; in the TUI pager these are folded into the `/hooks` modal."}]},{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.grok\\docs\\user-guide\\05-configuration.md","matches":[{"line_number":51,"content":"group_tool_verbs = true                # fold runs of read/search/list tool calls and subagent rows"},{"line_number":53,"content":"collapsed_edit_blocks = false          # show edits as one-line +N/-M diffstat summaries and merge"},{"line_number":56,"content":"                                       # expanded_by_default/line_summary override its fold shape)"},{"line_number":608,"content":"collapse_unfocused = true             # collapse prompt when scrollback is focused"},{"line_number":636,"content":"anchor_on_fold = true                 # keep block position when folding"},{"line_number":637,"content":"respect_manual_folds = true           # opt-in (default: false): keep manually folded blocks as-is during streaming/finish; expanding while following stops auto-scroll"},{"line_number":642,"content":"expandable_indicator = true           # show expand indicator on foldable entries"},{"line_number":649,"content":"dim_accent = 0.5                      # dimming factor for collapsed accents (0.0-1.0)"},{"line_number":652,"content":"`respect_manual_folds` is off by default. Turn it on and a block you fold by hand is pinned: streaming updates and finish events (a thinking block ending, say) leave its fold state alone, and expanding a block while follow-mode is tailing new content stops the auto-scroll so the view stays put. Follow resumes via `Shift+G`, `j` at the last entry, scrolling past the bottom, or sending a new prompt. `Shift+E` clears all pins; `Ctrl+E` clears pins on thinking blocks."},{"line_number":660,"content":"# expanded_by_default = true          # unset: follows [ui] collapsed_edit_blocks in config.toml"},{"line_number":661,"content":"                                      # (flag on = collapsed one-liner); uncomment to pin either shape"},{"line_number":663,"content":"# line_summary = false                # show +N/-M in the collapsed header; unset follows the same flag"}]},{"path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.grok\\docs\\user-guide\\06-theming.md","matches":[{"line_number":148,"content":"Grok bundles three `.tmTheme` files for code-block syntax highlighting and selects one based on the active theme:"},{"line_number":195,"content":"anchor_on_fold = true       # Keep block header at same screen position when folding"},{"line_number":204,"content":"expandable_indicator = true        # Show \"›\" on foldable collapsed entries"},{"line_number":206,"content":"collapsed_accent_char = \"❙\"        # Accent for collapsed groupable blocks (falls back to \"|\" on the legacy Windows console)"},{"line_number":226,"content":"# expanded_by_default = true    # Unset: follows [ui] collapsed_edit_blocks in config.toml"},{"line_number":227,"content":"                                # (flag on = collapsed one-liner); uncomment to pin either shape"},{"line_number":230,"content":"# line_summary = false          # Show +N/-M in the collapsed header; unset follows the same flag"}]}]}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":323672,"eventId":"019fab7f-7ed9-7553-a471-73b6cca96147-35427","agentTimestampMs":1785386988553,"promptId":"a3d9b45c-1f05-4403-9f5e-48cd4fe528c8","streamStartMs":1785386986011,"turnStartMs":1785386976678,"updateType":"ToolCallUpdate","updateParams":{"toolCallId":"call-3282ed69-9df3-4112-a2ab-8efaf80017c4-283","status":"Completed"}}}}
{"timestamp":1785386993,"method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"019fab7f-7ed9-7553-a471-73b6cca96147","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"I have clear documentation for how to collapse entries in Grok Build TUI."}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":324880,"eventId":"019fab7f-7ed9-7553-a471-73b6cca96147-35443","agentTimestampMs":1785386993941,"promptId":"a3d9b45c-1f05-4403-9f5e-48cd4fe528c8","streamStartMs":1785386992434,"turnStartMs":1785386976678,"updateType":"AgentThoughtChunk","chunkId":16}}}
{"timestamp":1785387001,"method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"019fab7f-7ed9-7553-a471-73b6cca96147","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_message_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"# 怎么折叠对话里的长内容（Grok Build TUI）\n\n先把焦点切到**上方面板（scrollback）**，再折叠：\n\n1. `Tab` 或 `Space`：从输入框切到历史消息区  \n2. `↑` / `↓`：选中某条消息 / 某块内容  \n3. **折叠 / 展开**\n\n| 操作 | 默认（Simple 模式） | Vim 模式 |\n|------|---------------------|----------|\n| 折叠当前条 | `←` | `h` |\n| 展开当前条 | `→` | `l` |\n| 切换折叠 | — | `e` |\n| 全部展开/全部折叠 | — | `Shift+E` |\n| 折叠/展开全部 thinking | `Ctrl+E` | 同左 |\n\n入口说明见用户指南：[Keyboard Shortcuts](file:///C:/Users/Administrator/.grok/docs/user-guide/03-keyboard-shortcuts.md) · [Getting Started](file:///C:/Users/Administrator/.grok/docs/user-guide/01-getting-started.md)\n\n---\n\n## 实用技巧\n\n- **只盯工具输出/长代码**：用方向键选中那一块 → `←` 折成一行  \n- **Vim 习惯**：`/vim-mode` 打开后，用 `h`/`l`/`e` 更顺手  \n- **不想折叠被流式更新顶开**：可在 pager 配置里开 `respect_manual_folds = true`（见配置文档）  \n- **长代码当全文看**：选中后 `Enter` 进全屏查看  \n\n---\n\n## 如果是「让我少贴长代码」\n\n那是输出习惯问题，不是 UI 折叠：可以说「以后长代码写进文件，对话里只给路径和摘要」，我会少贴大块代码。\n\n**一句话：** 焦点在历史区 → 选中那条 → **`←` 折叠 / `→` 展开**。"}},"_meta":{"totalTokens":324880,"eventId":"019fab7f-7ed9-7553-a471-73b6cca96147-35885","agentTimestampMs":1785387000737,"promptId":"a3d9b45c-1f05-4403-9f5e-48cd4fe528c8","streamStartMs":1785386992434,"turnStartMs":1785386976678,"updateType":"AgentMessageChunk","chunkId":458}}}
